{
  "pages": [
    {
      "page_idx": 17,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "footer",
          "bbox": [
            0.449,
            0.97,
            0.55,
            0.985
          ],
          "content": "Reprint 2026-27"
        },
        {
          "type": "header",
          "bbox": [
            0.586,
            0.046,
            0.862,
            0.064
          ],
          "content": "We Distribute, Yet Things Multiply"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.115,
            0.087,
            0.622,
            0.109
          ],
          "content": "？ How many square tiles are there in each figure?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.11,
            0.123,
            0.814,
            0.146
          ],
          "content": "How many are there in Step 4 of the sequence? What about Step 10?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.159,
            0.801,
            0.217
          ],
          "content": "？ Write an algebraic expression for the number of tiles in Step n. Share your methods with the class. Can you find more than one method to arrive at the answer?"
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.817,
            0.154,
            0.904,
            0.207
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_17_image_5.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.232,
            0.846,
            0.271
          ],
          "content": "？ Find the area of the (interior) shaded region in the figure below. All four rectangles have the same dimensions. m"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.276,
            0.339,
            0.294
          ],
          "content": "**Tadang’s method:**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.294,
            0.704,
            0.33
          ],
          "content": "The total region is a square of side (m + n) with an area $( m + n ) ^ { 2 }$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.331,
            0.704,
            0.387
          ],
          "content": "Subtracting the area of four rectangles from the total area will give the area of the interior shaded region. That is, $( m + n ) ^ { 2 } - 4 m n$"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.393,
            0.324,
            0.411
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Yusuf’s method:"
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.716,
            0.255,
            0.921,
            0.413
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_17_image_11.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.412,
            0.705,
            0.449
          ],
          "content": "The shaded region is a square with sidelength (n – m). So, its area is $( n - m ) ^ { 2 } .$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.109,
            0.458,
            0.465,
            0.482
          ],
          "content": "By expanding both expressions,"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.484,
            0.49,
            0.504
          ],
          "content": "check that $(m + n)^{2} - 4mn = (n - m)^{2}$ ."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.519,
            0.72,
            0.577
          ],
          "content": "? Find out the area of the region with slanting lines in the figure. All three rectangles have the same dimensions (Fig. 1)."
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.727,
            0.433,
            0.882,
            0.582
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [
            {
              "bbox": [
                0.797,
                0.587,
                0.84,
                0.602
              ],
              "content": "Fig. 1"
            }
          ],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_17_image_16.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.64,
            0.342,
            0.658
          ],
          "content": "**Anusha’s method:**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.658,
            0.579,
            0.678
          ],
          "content": "Required area = Area (ABCD) – Area (EFGH)"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.678,
            0.333,
            0.695
          ],
          "content": "Area of ABCD = x<sup>2</sup>."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.696,
            0.335,
            0.713
          ],
          "content": "Area of EFGH = xy."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.714,
            0.382,
            0.734
          ],
          "content": "Required $\\mathrm{arc} \\underline{a} = x^{2} - \\overline{x} y.$"
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.714,
            0.615,
            0.889,
            0.756
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_17_image_23.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.778,
            0.365,
            0.796
          ],
          "content": "**Vaishnavi’s method:**"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.332,
            0.797,
            0.464,
            0.832
          ],
          "content": "\\begin{array} { l } { { \\mathrm { Q S } = y + x + y } } \\\\ { { \\quad = x + 2 y . } } \\end{array}",
          "image_source": "images/page_17_equation_25.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.232,
            0.833,
            0.474,
            0.851
          ],
          "content": "Area of $PQSR = x(x + 2y)$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.852,
            0.708,
            0.889
          ],
          "content": "Required area = Area of PQSR – (area of the three rectangles)"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.31,
            0.888,
            0.476,
            0.908
          ],
          "content": "x \\left( x + 2y \\right) - 3xy.",
          "image_source": "images/page_17_equation_28.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.702,
            0.764,
            0.89,
            0.907
          ],
